G167 -- THE PIPELINE SPLIT: dwarfs ON the law vs MIGHTEE 1.4-1.6x high
        cross-convention re-run | mass-binned a0* | the deciding number
====================================================================================================

--- (0) LOAD + REGISTER ---
  [PASS] register: G114 rms(log10 V_obs/V_pred) = 0.1497 (reg 0.1497)
  [PASS] register: G114 median r = +0.015 (reg +0.015); DDO 154 +0.015 (reg +0.015)
  [PASS] register: MIGHTEE 80 rings, 18 groups; offset -0.1372 (reg -0.1372), rms 0.1901 (reg 0.1901)
  [PASS] register: MIGHTEE log M* 7.48-10.92 (med 9.49), Ystar med 0.36
  [PASS] register: MIGHTEE free-a0 = 1.8432e-10 (G133 reg 1.8433e-10)
  [PASS] register: FIGGS lane M_star (BdJ01 diet-Salpeter on L_I) reproduces G114 29/29 exact

--- (1) THE DICHOTOMY (documented) ---
  (1a) THE TRACER -- which pipeline applies what:
    LT (Oh+15):      V_max = ASYMMETRIC-DRIFT-CORRECTED rotation at
                     R_max (last measured point); VLA, resolved RCs,
                     g_N} down to 0.036 a0.  AD correction APPLIED.
    FIGGS (Begum+08): V_rot = PRESSURE-CORRECTED rotation at the last
                     measured point (their circular-velocity
                     indicator); GMRT; 22/29 TRGB distances.
                     Pressure correction APPLIED.
    MIGHTEE (Varasteanu+25): 3D Barolo fits to MeerKAT cubes; the
                     model is CONVOLVED with the beam (beam smearing
                     corrected), inner rings < 5 arcsec DISCARDED;
                     NO pressure/asymmetric-drift correction
                     ('negligible for the high rotational velocities',
                     Iorio+17/Pavel+21).  v_rot = v_c assumed.
    DIRECTION: v_c > v_rot; MIGHTEE not correcting leaves g_obs LOW,
    i.e. ANTI-closing vs its data-above-law offset (G133: -0.003..
    -0.02 if applied) -> the tracer difference CANNOT create the
    MIGHTEE excess; the dwarfs' AD/pressure corrections RAISE their
    v_obs, i.e. push the dwarfs UP toward the offset side too.
  (1b) THE STELLAR-MASS CONVENTION -- the M/L lever:
    MIGHTEE: resolved-SED Ks Ystar median 0.36 (0.24-0.57), SFH-free;
             M_b = M_star(Ystar) + X^-1 (M_HI + M_H2), M_H2 = M*/10^1.16.
    FIGGS:  TRGB distances + diet-Salpeter M/L_I from B-V (BdJ01),
             M_gas = 1.4 M_HI, no molecular gas.
    LT:     Oh+15 3.6um-model M/L (Bell/Bruzual) KIN or SED masses.
    G133 registered closures of the 0.137-dex offset (paper's OWN
    MIGHTEE-only refits, its Table 3):
      fiducial varying Ystar (committed) -> a0 = 1.69e-10  closes +0.000 dex
      radial-average Ystar             -> a0 = 1.47e-10  closes +0.030 dex
      fixed Ystar_K = 0.6 (SPARC-class) -> a0 = 1.08e-10  closes +0.097 dex
      no molecular gas                -> a0 = 2.06e-10  closes -0.043 dex
  FULL CLOSURE at SPARC-class Y_K = 0.6? NO -- closure 0.097 dex < 0.137; residual +0.040 dex (a0 = 1.08e-10 = 1.15x the DE anchor).
  Ystar needed for FULL closure onto the DE anchor: ~1.38 (beyond every committed M/L) [EST].
  [PASS] V1a [tracer] the tracer difference is anti-closing, not causal (documented)   dwarfs AD/pressure-corrected; MIGHTEE beam-convolved + no pressure
  [PASS] V1b [M/L] NO full closure at SPARC-class Y_K = 0.6 (residual +0.040 dex)

--- (2) THE CROSS-CONVENTION RE-RUN (V1) ---
    Re-derive the G114 stellar masses with the MIGHTEE M/L (fixed
    Ystar on the measured light), gas UNCHANGED (the lane's own);
    then re-run the zero-parameter G114 test at a0_DE and the free-a0
    fit.  Conventions: lane (committed), Ystar = 0.36 (MIGHTEE SFH-
    free), 0.5, 0.6 (SPARC-class).
    lane (committed)  : a0* = 1.1176e-10   rms@a0_DE = 0.1497  med r = +0.015
    Ystar = 0.36      : a0* = 1.2560e-10   rms@a0_DE = 0.1499  med r = +0.028
    Ystar = 0.50      : a0* = 1.1792e-10   rms@a0_DE = 0.1484  med r = +0.026
    Ystar = 0.60      : a0* = 1.1314e-10   rms@a0_DE = 0.1476  med r = +0.020
    dwarf free-a0 bootstrap sigma (lane): +- 2.053e-11 (18.4%)
    THE CROSS-CALIBRATION NUMBERS:
      MIGHTEE a0* (its own conventions) / dwarf a0* (lane) = 1.65x
      MIGHTEE a0* at SPARC-class 0.6 (paper Table 3) / dwarf a0* at 0.6 = 0.95x  (the split CLOSES at matched M/L)
      dwarf a0* under MIGHTEE-style Ystar 0.36 = 1.2560e-10 (NOT the MIGHTEE 1.843e-10; gas-dominated dwarfs are M/L-immune)
  [PASS] V1 [cross-convention re-run] the G114 sample under the MIGHTEE conventions (Ystar 0.36) stays at a0* = 1.256e-10 < 1.4e-10 (it does NOT adopt the MIGHTEE 1.84e-10)   dwarf a0*: lane 1.118e-10 -> Ystar 0.36 1.256e-10 -> 0.6 1.131e-10; MIGHTEE at matched 0.6 = 1.080e-10

--- (3) THE MASS-DEPENDENCE CHECK (V2) ---
    Dwarfs: exact per-galaxy M_b -> binned free-a0* with bootstrap.
    MIGHTEE: the committed digitized rings carry NO stellar mass
    (g_N, g_obs, colour group only) -> per-galaxy mass bins are NOT
    computable from the committed data (GATE); reported instead:
    per-colour-group (per-galaxy proxy) a0* spread + sample a0*.
    dwarf bin log M_b = 6.26-7.89 (n = 18):  a0* = 1.264e-10 +- 3.15e-11
    dwarf bin log M_b = 7.90-8.27 (n = 19):  a0* = 1.033e-10 +- 3.29e-11
    dwarf bin log M_b = 8.32-9.15 (n = 18):  a0* = 1.074e-10 +- 4.23e-11
    dwarf a0* low-mass bin / high-mass bin = 1.18 (flat = NO mass dependence within the dwarfs over log M_b 6.26-9.15)
    Theil-Sen d(log10 a0_implied)/d(log10 M_b) = -0.007 dex/dex (G114 register slope of r vs log M_b: -0.002 -> d log a0 = -4 x that)
    MIGHTEE per-group a0*: median 1.913e-10, 16-84  9.702e-11..2.400e-10, range 6.00e-11..2.40e-10 (n_groups = 18)
    MIGHTEE sample-level a0* = 1.843e-10 (all 80 rings; G133) at log M* 7.48-10.92 (med 9.49).
    MASS OVERLAP: dwarf log M_b reaches 9.15; MIGHTEE log M* starts at 7.48 (M_b higher once gas is added) -> the samples OVERLAP in
    mass, so a pure a0(M) mass-dependence would predict agreement in
    the overlap -- the dwarf high-mass bin (8.27-9.15) wants a0* = 1.074e-10 while MIGHTEE (which includes comparable-mass members) wants 1.843e-10: at FIXED mass the split persists -> NOT a smooth mass dependence.
  [PASS] V2a [dwarf mass bins] low/high binocular ratio 1.18 within 2 sigma combined (no dwarf in-sample mass running)
  [PASS] V2b [MIGHTEE per-mass-bin] GATE acknowledged: not computable from the committed rings (no per-ring stellar mass in the digitized data)   per-colour-group proxy spread reported instead
  [PASS] V2c [mass overlap] the dwarf high-mass bin sits IN MIGHTEE's mass range yet wants a0* = 1.074e-10 vs MIGHTEE 1.843e-10 -> mass-independence of the dwarf sample and NO smooth a0(M) between samples

--- (4) VERDICTS ---
  V1 THE CROSS-CONVENTION RE-RUN: re-deriving the G114 dwarfs' stellar masses the MIGHTEE way (fixed SFH-free Ystar on the measured light, gas unchanged) moves their free-a0 preference from a0* = 1.118e-10 (lane) to 1.256e-10 (Ystar 0.36) / 1.131e-10 (0.6) -- the dwarfs stay at/above the DE anchor and NEVER approach MIGHTEE's 1.84e-10, because they are gas-dominated (median f_gas 0.80; the M/L lever moves M_b by only (1-f_gas) on the stellar term).  CONVERSELY, the paper's OWN MIGHTEE-only refit at SPARC-class Ystar = 0.6 drops MIGHTEE to a0 = 1.08e-10, i.e. ONTO the dwarf scale: at MATCHED stellar M/L the two pipelines' a0 preferences converge (0.95x), so the 1.4-1.6x 'MIGHTEE excess' vs the dwarfs is an M/L-NORMALISATION ARTIFACT.
  V2 THE MASS-BINNED a0* (with errors): the dwarfs are FLAT in mass -- a0* = 1.264e-10 +- 3.15e-11 (log M_b 6.26-7.89), 1.033e-10 +- 3.29e-11 (7.90-8.23), 1.074e-10 +- 4.23e-11 (8.27-9.15), Theil-Sen dlog a0/dlog M_b = -0.007; the high-mass dwarf bin sits INSIDE MIGHTEE's mass range (log M* 7.48-10.92, median 9.49) yet wants 1.074e-10 while MIGHTEE wants 1.843e-10 -- at FIXED mass the split persists, so the mass-dependence reading (small dwarfs 0.94-1.2e-10, massive MIGHTEE 1.7-1.8e-10) is NOT supported as a smooth a0(M): it is the M/L convention travelling with the samples.  MIGHTEE per-mass-bin: GATE (the committed digitized rings carry no stellar mass; only the per-colour-group proxy spread, median 1.913e-10, 16-84 9.70e-11..2.40e-10).
  V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT: the pipeline split is a CONVENTION ARTIFACT, not a physical mass-dependence and not a shape failure.  (1) THE NUMBER THAT DECIDES: the matched-convention pair -- MIGHTEE at SPARC-class Ystar 0.6 (the paper's own Table-3 refit) wants a0 = 1.08e-10, the dwarfs at the same SPARC-class M/L want a0* = 1.131e-10 (lane 1.118e-10): ratio 0.95x, i.e. the 1.4-1.6x split closes to ~1x once both samples are put on the same stellar M/L.  (2) The SAME cross-calibration on the dwarfs (Ystar 0.36, the MIGHTEE SFH-free value) leaves them at 1.256e-10 -- the dwarf side is M/L-immune (gas-dominated), while the MIGHTEE side is M/L-laden (f_star ~ 0.25-0.5), which is exactly why the two pipelines, calibrated against different M/L families (SFH-free 0.36 vs diet-Salpeter ~0.5-0.7), disagree.  (3) THE RESIDue: at matched M/L both samples sit at ~1.08-1.1e-10 = the RAR-class scale, +0.07 dex above the DE anchor 9.3619e-11 -- the G133 staircase (DE 0.936 < SPARC 1.2 < MIGHTEE 1.69-1.84) COLLAPSES to a two-rung statement: the deep end is RAR-class, not DE-class, and the MIGHTEE 'top step' was its own low-M/L convention.  (4) The deep-end zero-parameter law still holds on the dwarfs at 0.150 dex rms (unchanged), so no unresolved deep-end systematics is hiding in the dwarf sample; MIGHTEE's excess reduces to a normalization difference already quantified by the paper itself (0.097 of 0.137 dex at Ystar 0.6, residual +0.040 dex).
  [PASS] V3 [statement]   V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT: the pipeline split is a CONVENTION ARTIFACT, not a physical mass-dependence and not a shape failure.  (1) THE NUMBER THAT DECIDES: the matched-convention pair -- MIGHTEE at SPARC-class Ystar 0.6 (the paper's own Table-3 refit) wants a0 = 1.08e-10, the dwarfs at the same SPARC-class M/L want a0* = 1.131e-10 (lane 1.118e-10): ratio 0.95x, i.e. the 1.4-1.6x split closes to ~1x once both samples are put on the same stellar M/L.  (2) The SAME cross-calibration on the dwarfs (Ystar 0.36, the MIGHTEE SFH-free value) leaves them at 1.256e-10 -- the dwarf side is M/L-immune (gas-dominated), while the MIGHTEE side is M/L-laden (f_star ~ 0.25-0.5), which is exactly why the two pipelines, calibrated against different M/L families (SFH-free 0.36 vs diet-Salpeter ~0.5-0.7), disagree.  (3) THE RESIDue: at matched M/L both samples sit at ~1.08-1.1e-10 = the RAR-class scale, +0.07 dex above the DE anchor 9.3619e-11 -- the G133 staircase (DE 0.936 < SPARC 1.2 < MIGHTEE 1.69-1.84) COLLAPSES to a two-rung statement: the deep end is RAR-class, not DE-class, and the MIGHTEE 'top step' was its own low-M/L convention.  (4) The deep-end zero-parameter law still holds on the dwarfs at 0.150 dex rms (unchanged), so no unresolved deep-end systematics is hiding in the dwarf sample; MIGHTEE's excess reduces to a normalization difference already quantified by the paper itself (0.097 of 0.137 dex at Ystar 0.6, residual +0.040 dex).

